    "body": "### What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nEvaluation and serving usually need BF16 Hugging Face weights, not FSDP's full FP32 master weights. Today users must save verl checkpoint shards and run the [offline FSDP merger](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/verl/model_merger/fsdp_model_merger.py#L53-L83), which consumes verl checkpoint shards rather than an already exported HF safetensors model. This PR adds `hf_export_dtype` (`bf16`, `fp16`, or `fp32`) to cast only the HF export before [`save_pretrained`](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/main/src/transformers/modeling_utils.py#L3235-L3248); `null` preserves current behavior.\r\n\r\nRelated to #296. This does not duplicate #7997: that PR forwards Transformers `save_pretrained` kwargs, but Transformers has no save-time dtype conversion argument. Open-PR searches for `hf_export_dtype`, `export checkpoint dtype`, and #296 found no PR implementing export-only dtype conversion.\r\n\r\nFixes one part of https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues/8027\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Starting\r\n\r\n- [x] Search for similar PRs: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+hf_export_dtype\r\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}`.\r\n\r\n### API and Usage Example\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# PPO actor with FSDP or VeOmni\r\nactor_rollout_ref.actor.checkpoint.hf_export_dtype=bf16\r\n\r\n# SFT with engine=fsdp or engine=veomni\r\ncheckpoint.hf_export_dtype=bf16\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Test\r\n\r\nSix 8-GPU training runs with `Qwen/Qwen3-8B` verified `hf_export_dtype=null` and `hf_export_dtype=bf16` across FSDP actor, SFT, and VeOmni actor. Each run used FP32 model initialization and master parameters, BF16 mixed-precision compute, and one training step. Every export contained the expected `8,190,735,360` parameters and reloaded through Transformers:\r\n\r\n| Path | Default | `bf16` | HF reload |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| FSDP actor | FP32, 1 file | BF16, 1 file | Passed |\r\n| SFT | FP32, 1 file | BF16, 1 file | Passed |\r\n| VeOmni actor | FP32, 1 file | BF16, 1 file | Passed |\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Submitting\r\n\r\n- [x] Read the Contribute Guide.\r\n- [x] Apply relevant pre-commit checks.\r\n- [x] Add / update documentation.\r\n- [x] Test coverage considered: no permanent test was added because this is a small export-only conversion. The multi-GPU runs above verified `null` and `bf16` across FSDP, SFT, and VeOmni end to end.\r\n- [ ] Send a message in `ci-request` after human review and once this draft is ready for CI.\r\n- [x] This PR does not touch the `recipe` submodule.\r\n\r\nAI assistance from OpenAI Codex was used for code-path analysis, implementation, validation, experiment orchestration, and PR drafting. All code changes have been reviewed by me.\r\n",
